{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1282797-true-faith-and-banality","id":1282797,"title":"True Faith and Banality.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-01-25T23:15:11-08:00","id":1282797,"title":"True Faith and Banality.","content":"So I'm thinking about using the Renewal in Faith Fellowship from c20(aka the pray the fae away&quot; autumn folk). And I was think of stacking Some True Faith on top of autumn folk stigma, to better represent a break between &quot;believing in the supernatural&quot; and being a source of glamour/banality. But generally as people can see from my threads on True Faith I have a profoundly negative view on it.. so I'd like to get perspectives on the other side. From those who see True Faith as a more &quot;unalloyed good&quot; does having an Autumn person with True faith sort of violate your head cannon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T06:49:04-08:00","id":1283033,"title":"","content":"Interesting thought. Now, True Faith is one of those things I believe everyone has a different take on.<br /> It basically is the idea that you follow a religious creed with personal sincereness and investment. You actually believe what you do is what your god(s) want and it is at least so much in line with that religions morals and creeds, that it profits from the collective thought put into this religion. (I'm coming from a Mage-y perspective here.) So having a rather fundamentalist christian view, that regards supernaturals, especially Fae as demons is possible and would not violate my headcannon. True Faith is not &quot;good&quot; or &quot;evil&quot;. And while someone who is very invested in the moral side of christian religion can manifest it, the more fundamental and extremist sides can also use this power.<br /> Now, how does True Faith correspond to Banality? A fundamentalist view denying the existence of Fey and regarding them as demons that are to be banned to hell is very much possible. It is the closed mindedness that defines this world view, both in Banality and this particular flavour of True Faith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T08:04:49-08:00","id":1283048,"title":"","content":"Yeah, saying someone with a fundamentalist (in the general sense instead of a specific denomination) view can't have True Faith would seem even more insulting to people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T08:38:12-08:00","id":1283056,"title":"","content":"Person can be creative and imaginative even if they truly believe and have True Faith or they can be the most restrictive, uncreative, boring and dull yet still believe in a greater power and have True Faith. So there may be Dreamers with True Faith and there can be Autumn people with True Faith.<br /> <br /> Personally I do not attach morality to True Faith, it is neither good or evil, as I personally feel it is about the persons belief not anything else. There are those who torture people in the name of their God and wield True Faith and there are those who make pledge their lives to helping others and wield True Faith both may even have True Faith in the same God. And at my table as it is the Faith that matters True Faith can be wielded by those believing in other Gods than those of Abrahamic <br /> <br /> But more than most things Faith is truly a matter where YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T11:04:01-08:00","id":1283078,"title":"","content":"Recall that the most in-depth treatment of True Faith ever published was in the pages of <b>The Inquisition</b>, a <b>Vampire</b> supplement describing a fanatical religious order that hunts and destroys vampires, and frequently goes overboard while doing so. True Faith does not mean morally upstanding. <br /> <br /> But it's not opposed to it, either: the faithful needn't be zealous bigots blinded by their faith; they can also be presented as visionaries whose faith empowers then to seek a better future or as bringers of mercy who are more concerned with easing suffering than in smiting the wicked. Heck, even zeal can be a good thing, giving the faithful the determination to keep going even when nothing is going your way. <br /> <br /> So too with the relationship between True Faith and Banality: they're on different axes, and someone with True Faith can either be high Banality (emphasizing the worst tendencies of Faith to lead to rigid adherence) or low Banality (emphasizing Faith's ability to inspire you).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T18:00:20-08:00","id":1283150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1282797-true-faith-and-banality#post1282797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm thinking about using the Renewal in Faith Fellowship from c20(aka the pray the fae away&quot; autumn folk). And I was think of stacking Some True Faith on top of autumn folk stigma, to better represent a break between &quot;believing in the supernatural&quot; and being a source of glamour/banality. But generally as people can see from my threads on True Faith I have a profoundly negative view on it.. so I'd like to get perspectives on the other side. From those who see True Faith as a more &quot;unalloyed good&quot; does having an Autumn person with True faith sort of violate your head cannon?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Personally, I'm very skeptical about the concept that True Faith would oppose Glamour, rather than fuel it. Religious doctrine is cram packed with fantastical stories of myths and legends, and if somebody believes in that hard enough to manifest supernatural abilities, it makes absolutely no sense why they would be depicted as autumn people.<br /> <br /> It's like people who claim to believe in an afterlife, but then turn around and say that <i>&quot;ghosts aren't real!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> I feel like if you believe in the existence of a soul, you have to, by extension, believe in the possibility of lingering spirits.<br /> <br /> Same logic applies to the existence of magic, monsters and (most importantly) the Dreaming. If you believe some of these things can exist, what's preventing you from entertaining the possibility that others might exist as well?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-27-2019, 09:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T18:28:58-08:00","id":1283156,"title":"","content":"I am not saying &quot;EVERYONE&quot; with True Faith is an Autumn Person. I am saying a certain take of fundimentalist Christianity is the perfect mix of Autumn Person Banality and True Faith(aka the Pray the Fae Away conversion camps).<br /> <br /> That i don't believe belief in the supernatural is intrinsically Glamourous any more than belief in Science is intrinsically Banal. I mean from a setting perspective the lowest point of Glamour was the transition in the High Middle Ages/Enlightenment period.. and there was PLENTY of belief in the supernatural then.. it was just sort of taken for Granted. From the Descriptions of Trods glamour seems to have regenerated in part over time making the Ressurgence less of a Fluke.<br /> <br /> A person who's world is dark and grey without joy, without fear just a mindless &quot;acceptance&quot;. That's what I'm imagining here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T18:33:05-08:00","id":1283158,"title":"","content":"Glamour isn't about believing in the supernatural, and Banality isn't about not believing in it. Banality is about focusing on what you're supposed to do and ignoring whimsy and whatnot, while Glamour is about passion and creativity. C20 makes it pretty clear on that.<br /> <br /> If you have True Faith be both (so the question really becomes if anyone from that branch of Christianity can have True Faith, which I say yes to but some disagree), then someone with True Faith can have any Banality rating, including being a Dreamer or an Autumn person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T18:47:24-08:00","id":1283160,"title":"","content":"So Banality is focused apathy? A choice to reject everything outside of your role? Sameness over novelty?<br /> <br /> Banality has always been a little unclear, so I like to check every chance I get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T18:49:08-08:00","id":1283161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1282797-true-faith-and-banality?p=1283160#post1283160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Banality is focused apathy? A choice to reject everything outside of your role? Sameness over novelty?<br /> <br /> Banality has always been a little unclear, so I like to check every chance I get.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That's the interpretation I'm going with. I can't imagine Conversion camps being anything but banal or Ravaging..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T18:51:13-08:00","id":1283162,"title":"","content":"Changeling the Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition does a really really good job explaining Banality starting on page 267. I find the explanations for each level the most helpful part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T22:15:16-08:00","id":1283196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1282797-true-faith-and-banality?p=1283158#post1283158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glamour isn't about believing in the supernatural, and Banality isn't about not believing in it. Banality is about focusing on what you're supposed to do and ignoring whimsy and whatnot, while Glamour is about passion and creativity. C20 makes it pretty clear on that.<br /> <br /> If you have True Faith be both (so the question really becomes if anyone from that branch of Christianity can have True Faith, which I say yes to but some disagree), then someone with True Faith can have any Banality rating, including being a Dreamer or an Autumn person.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That could make sense. I came across a video some time ago which went into detail about how the advent of Christianity in Europe actually lead to people being less artistically creative for roughly 1,500 years. (thanks a lot, House Liam...)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> On the concept of believing in the supernatural allowing for Banality, you could explain it as perceiving Fae and the like as just another part of the world that people have to deal with every day.<br /> <br /> Conversely, the Glamour of science could stem from the fascination with overcoming the odds and exploring new possibilities","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T12:15:44-08:00","id":1283323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1282797-true-faith-and-banality?p=1283196#post1283196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That could make sense. I came across a video some time ago which went into detail about how the advent of Christianity in Europe actually lead to people being less artistically creative for roughly 1,500 years. (thanks a lot, House Liam...)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> On the concept of believing in the supernatural allowing for Banality, you could explain it as perceiving Fae and the like as just another part of the world that people have to deal with every day.<br /> <br /> Conversely, the Glamour of science could stem from the fascination with overcoming the odds and exploring new possibilities</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wouldn't go so far as that. There's plenty of art from the Medieval period. Its not an &quot;all Religion is soul Crushing&quot; its that particular takes are soul Crushing. Now the particular Modern &quot;God of the Gaps&quot; interpretation of God who tries to force the issue of Religion vs Science I feel is particularly Banal. They have put their god in a tiny little box and anything outside it they scream as impossible. They demand the miraculous as expection rather than a joyous gift. They force conformity rather than novelty.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T09:53:11-08:00","id":1285938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1282797-true-faith-and-banality?p=1283323#post1283323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I wouldn't go so far as that. There's plenty of art from the Medieval period. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>True, but compared to art from the periods that came before (and after) it (such as the Roman empire and the Renaissance era), the art of the medieval period is generically bland, and caters to an idealized version of what Christianity wanted to see in the world. But the Greeks and Romans had been producing art that depicted the world in a far more realistic style, and in doing so, it was far more inspiring to the people at the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T19:50:17-08:00","id":1286073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1282797-true-faith-and-banality?p=1285938#post1285938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, but compared to art from the periods that came before (and after) it (such as the Roman empire and the Renaissance era), the art of the medieval period is generically bland, and caters to an idealized version of what Christianity wanted to see in the world. But the Greeks and Romans had been producing art that depicted the world in a far more realistic style, and in doing so, it was far more inspiring to the people at the time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not really? Unless you start saying things like Charlemange and the Crusades aren't Medieval. If you're only counting say the Migration period in Western Europe...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T20:03:27-08:00","id":1286076,"title":"","content":"I don't know what I was thinking there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10243,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","user":"zenten","date":".  What I said was very incorrect, and served no purpose. 02-13-2019, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T08:45:48-08:00","id":1287547,"title":"","content":"My grandmother has True Faith. She uses it benignly and benevolently, has accepted my transition and my cousin's trans identity. She believes everyone, no matter skin color, creed or identity and orientation, is deserving of respect and rights. She keeps her opinions to herself and doesn't judge anyone harshly, as she feels God's provenance is judgment and she is not God. (We joke that God's afraid she'll take over if she gets to Heaven and she's too good for Hell, so she's functionally immortal, but that's besides the point). <br /> <br /> Another family member has True Faith. They use it to decry ethnic identity and gender identity and sexual orientation as aberrant and evil. They are ultracon zealots who even believe that the True Church was derailed by Jews in the 1940s and that the Antichrist walks amongst us. <br /> <br /> True Faith is irrespective of morality. Autumn People with True Faith can be made more dangerous. Allies with True Faith can be made more helpful and benevolent. It's not a broad blanket thing. It's case by case and group by group. <br /> <br /> (Also, cheers to the Renewal In Faith antags! I was hoping they'd get some use. ^_^ )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-15T06:15:18-07:00","id":1305027,"title":"","content":"A very interesting conversation indeed. So happy everyone here is respectful of each other. A rare treat.<br /> <br /> As for True Faith, Glamour and ones Spiritual Compass; It is the view of some esoteric philosophies (and apparently the original White Wolf staff) that it it Materialism that is the true corrupting force in the universe. This includes a love of material possessions <i>and </i>an inability to perceive a greater purpose or meaning in anything. Sort of a metaphysical depression that crushes out everything in reality until all that remains is empty, dead matter.<br /> <br /> In this vein we can view the more close-minded and crushing forms of religious and secular societies as inherently banal. If such belief and society crushes out, or disregards passion, pain and purpose, they rob existence of its deeper connection to everyone and everything around them, and is banal. If faith grows and encourages empathy, connection and purpose, it elevates the spirit over the material. And that seems pretty Glamour rich to me.<br /> <br /> I am also put in mind that in Christian history, the greatest teachers, church fathers and just about all of the major persons in the Bible were outcasts from their respective societies. Time spent in the wilderness seems part of the deal, and big organized Churches inherently corrupting. In other faiths such as Buddhism and Islam, this is also the case.<br /> <br /> My thoughts anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 04-15-2019, 10:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactio